{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1084992-how-do-you-do-that-transform-kinain-into-kithain","id":1084992,"title":"How Do You Do That? Transform Kinain into Kithain","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-28T06:12:18-07:00","id":1084992,"title":"How Do You Do That? Transform Kinain into Kithain","content":"What sort of spheres would you need to transform a Kinain into a Kithain? We never really got clear cut rules for constructing or altering spirits and this is one that bugged me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T06:50:47-07:00","id":1085001,"title":"","content":"&quot;constructing or altering spirits &quot; It's Spirit/DimSci 5. VE: Convention book has rules to create aliens.<br /> <br /> However, this it's not the same as what you're asking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T08:13:11-07:00","id":1085037,"title":"","content":"Still, Aleph's answer makes sense. I'd suggest a combo of Spirit 5 and Prime 5, your making a significant change in the cosmos with the proposed change. I'd also suggest that it would require some kind of contact with higher powers in the Dreaming, a very long ritual, and lots of Tass and Glamour. And these seem to be minimum requirements to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T11:01:14-07:00","id":1085077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1084992-how-do-you-do-that-transform-kinain-into-kithain?p=1085037#post1085037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, Aleph's answer makes sense. I'd suggest a combo of Spirit 5 and Prime 5, your making a significant change in the cosmos with the proposed change. I'd also suggest that it would require some kind of contact with higher powers in the Dreaming, a very long ritual, and lots of Tass and Glamour. And these seem to be minimum requirements to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both of you had helpful info. I am now thinking of a ritual where a Kinain is linked to a number of individuals and if they can each attain Rapture, turn Autumn people into Dreamers, and lower the local Banality ratings in enough places, they can concentrate the resurgence in the Dreaming into the Kinain subject who eventually is transformed into a Kithain.<br /> <br /> Edit: This would of course be Spirit 5, along with some Correspondence 3 thrown in to tie the different participants together. Maybe Prime 3 as well to ensure proper distribution of energy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 04-28-2017, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T11:05:48-07:00","id":1085079,"title":"","content":"*************","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T16:01:26-07:00","id":1085204,"title":"","content":"It's going to take more than application of Spheres, it's going to take a STORY. You want to turn a mortal into one of the fae. That's what they are, living stories.<br /> <br /> Saying &quot;I sip my G&amp;T before I toss it on the dude, flip my personal focus plastic lighter and light him on fire for a Spirit 5/Prime 5 effect&quot; isn't going to turn a Kinain into a Kithain. It's going to warp the Kinain into a Kithain facsimile. Who might be able to go into the Dreaming and do a Pinnochio story analogue to become a &quot;real&quot; fae.<br /> <br /> It would probably be easier to catalyze a Chrysalis. (That's certainly a story... the son of a fairy who meets a wizard who casts a spell and reveals his true self...) It would probably even be easier, though not easy, to get a fae from the Dreaming and &quot;sidhe&quot; it into the Kinain, though that would displace the soul to wherever it is that those souls went.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 04-29-2017, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T16:10:36-07:00","id":1085210,"title":"","content":"I was thinking of multiple stories. Like each person involved does something incredible to aid The Dreaming and as the Dreaming grows stronger the Kinain's Fae side grows stronger. Almost like a pact with the Dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T16:20:05-07:00","id":1085215,"title":"","content":"Or just dig into myths and stories? Something a little less conditional than Oisin so he doesn't stop being a changeling when he gets off his horse. More like dipping Achilles into the Styx. Or Demeter cooking Demephon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 04-28-2017, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T16:14:04-07:00","id":1085615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1084992-how-do-you-do-that-transform-kinain-into-kithain?p=1085001#post1085001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;constructing or altering spirits &quot; It's Spirit/DimSci 5. VE: Convention book has rules to create aliens.<br /> <br /> However, this it's not the same as what you're asking.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Was that Revised or M20?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T16:45:17-07:00","id":1085622,"title":"","content":"Technically, Revised. Void Engineers Convention book was published pretty close to M20, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T23:17:18-07:00","id":1085718,"title":"","content":"Considering the Dreaming isn't making new Kithain that they are eternal immortal faeries that can only be obliterated by banality and Iron.. Now you could hollow out the body and stuff in some sort of dream creature it might even have the memories of that person but it won't be that person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T18:15:06-07:00","id":1085982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1084992-how-do-you-do-that-transform-kinain-into-kithain?p=1085718#post1085718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the Dreaming isn't making new Kithain that they are eternal immortal faeries that can only be obliterated by banality and Iron.. Now you could hollow out the body and stuff in some sort of dream creature it might even have the memories of that person but it won't be that person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically it was the Tuathaan or humanity that made the Fae. And I believe that the Fae have made new Fae by sex since the trace their lineages. It shouldn't be impossible to make new Fae, simply difficult since the Dreaming has a mind of<br /> It's own and it doesn't like wizards messing with it.<br /> <br /> And if it's the latest Void book, which page?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T21:09:57-07:00","id":1086046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1084992-how-do-you-do-that-transform-kinain-into-kithain?p=1085982#post1085982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically it was the Tuathaan or humanity that made the Fae. And I believe that the Fae have made new Fae by sex since the trace their lineages. It shouldn't be impossible to make new Fae, simply difficult since the Dreaming has a mind of<br /> It's own and it doesn't like wizards messing with it.<br /> <br /> And if it's the latest Void book, which page?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, fae aren't making new fae sexually. They could before the Shattering. There is now a limited number of faerie souls. Period. They generally do recycle. Making a New Fae is on par with making a new vampire without kindred blood or a whole new Changing breed. Its a super big deal.<br /> <br /> Adhene do seem to be able to reproduce(and are not immortal) and one breed is made by extended interaction with the Dreaming on some level... so if you ripped out their soul while they were in the Dreaming you could make a Kemet","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","user":"Lian","date":". 05-01-2017, 12:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T11:32:43-07:00","id":1086269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if it's the latest Void book, which page?</div> </div> </div> </div>Umm...itr seems that my memory was somewhat wrong. They mention creating &quot;extradimensional entities&quot; in &quot;Cosmogenesis&quot; of p. 83 of that book and in M20 it's says the same but clearer (&quot;engineer custom-designed and constructed EDE organisms. She must employ Primal Utility energies as well (often including Life and Matter if the EDE construct is to survive outside the subdimensions\u2026 that is, if it\u2019s going to be more than simple ephemera)&quot;), but they never give a clear <i>system </i>for that.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, it's Spirit 5 + whatever you think you need (Prime 5 it's a good suggestion) + whatever deals with/whitin the Dreaming are appropiate to create the real deal instead of just a glamour laden immitation. As Lian says, &quot;Its a super big deal&quot;.<br /> To use the analogy of &quot;making a new vampire without kindred blood&quot;, as Tremere discovered, it's more feasible to just &quot;tap&quot;, and then redefine, the Curse of Caine to create a new Bloodline than to reinvent the wheel and create a new Caine...and that still was a big deal.<br /> In a similar (but appropiately different) fashion, you should tap into whatever &quot;Mythic Thread&quot; empowers the Faires. This will take more than just Lore, probably a lot of research about Faes, coupled with seekings within the Dreaming would be mandatory to even begin to understand the process implied&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-01-2017, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T15:31:29-07:00","id":1086359,"title":"","content":"I am already partly doing that by focusing on Kinain who are already partly Fae and can even learn Realms and Cantrips. Next I am focusing on not merely transmuting a Fae soul but feeding and nurturing the Dreaming and focusing the surge on a Kinain so that it can become a complete Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 05-01-2017, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T04:57:04-07:00","id":1086553,"title":"","content":"In my games, the Fey, Chimera and everything related to the Dreaming are effected by the Mind-Sphere instead of Spirit. I use the same rules as for spirits, just swap the spheres. Effectively this also means Glamour is just a form of Quintessence, modyfied by the Dreaming, so you would need both Prime and Mind to manipulate it. Since the Dreaming is thought-stuff, it makes just much more sense this way.<br /> So to modify a Kinain or Kithain soul... that's another thing. For the soul you'll definetly need Spirit at Level 5, also Prime, but to affect a Kinain, you also need the hight levels of Mind and the expertise of affecting a pattern like this, so Life in this case (as in: you can only do with Spirit/Mind in the Umbra/Dreaming, what you can already do with Pattern-Spheres in the material world).<br /> <br /> Also, there's always an increase of difficulty, when handling prodigals/supernaturals. If they accept you trying to change them it doesn't matter, but if they resist add a +3 modifier to the difficulty or roll their glamor or willpower against the effect (resisted roll).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T07:23:50-07:00","id":1086618,"title":"","content":"(Just jumping in...)<br /> <br /> Previous writers-hitting-the-forums from about 15 years ago (plus the cross-over stuff given in the ST Handbook) suggested that Mind and Spirit were necessary for Fae manipulation (though not always, depending on specific effect; Life/Mind were suggested for a number of things). To &quot;elevate&quot;, in a true/permanent manner, a Kinain into a Kithain (and assuming one is not wanting to use the guidelines for Arch-Spheres from the 90s), then Prime:5, Mind:5, Spirit:5 and Life:4 (assuming a physical manifestation is desired, which requires altering the target's physiology to a degree; if wholesale alteration is required, then Life:5) would be required, along with a shit-ton of successes, a given amount of Quintessence and/or (preferably) Tass with the appropriate resonance (such as would have a connection to both the Mundane World as well as to The Dreaming -- this is more likely to be found in places like the British Isles, and/or by making certain... sacrifices... of those who possess/carry Fae Blood, such as those with the appropriate Merit). How many successes/Q/T would be required depends on the setting/specific metaphysics in play for a given ST's world/time period. For the early 21st century, likely at least 50-100 successes (as you would be forging a new metaphysical essence, bonding it to a physical/living form, and doing so in an Age(tm) wherein such metaphysical shenanigans is nigh unto impossible (as it would be similar to creating a new type of vampire sans vitae, a new changing breed, or similar). If earlier (particularly at least during the Victorian Era, or even better during the pre-Renaissance), it's &quot;easier&quot; but things like Paradigm(tm) become something the ST should really, really be harder on than in current times. (Using the DA, official mages, likely only The Old Faith or some Valdaermen would have the knowledge/wisdom to know how to do something like this... and, as is often the case when poetic irony comes into play, they are the mages who would be least likely to *want* to perform such a feat as many of them have at least passing connections to many fae beings in the first place and wouldn't need to perform &quot;x&quot; in the first place.)<br /> <br /> And, of course, it goes without saying that even if executed properly this sort of magic(k) is <i>highly Vulgar </i>and likely to become subject to Disbelief over time, if not outright undone by Paradox spirits who determine this to be too offensive to Reality(tm) over time.<br /> <br /> Still, though, it *could* be done... it's just a question of &quot;Is it worth the blood, sweat and likely tears to make it happen...&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T09:58:57-07:00","id":1086680,"title":"","content":"All of what John said. And that's just the mechanical aspects. The parts that have to be played out using Focus are going to be just as complex and convoluted.<br /> <br /> Considering DA Fae as a template, probably the easiest way to do it would be to use minimal amounts of Mage magic at all. &quot;Changelings&quot; (as an Origin) could be humans that were abducted by the fae and kept around long enough for their human soul to change, with the missing bits &quot;filled in&quot; with fae energies or whatnot. So, technically, it might just take the ability to go into the Deep Dreaming, find an appropriately powerful True Fae and leave the character there with said entity to marinate forever and a day (or no time at all... there may not be much difference). I mean, it's probably going to end up something like a Changeling the Lost character in many ways, including the whole experience breaking the new changeling in all sorts of interesting ways (and by &quot;interesting&quot; I mean &quot;probably tragic&quot; for those who knew him or her before the mage went off and sold their friend to the whims of the most darkly whimsical imaginable beings...)<br /> <br /> Then all it would take is the appropriate Spheres to get into the Deep Dreaming. Or just making friends with a changeling who can get you there, no mage magic needed at all. <br /> <br /> But that's a LOT easier than doing something than Tremere tried to do and he was taking more shortcuts (using already extant vampire blood) than just &quot;making a new fae with magic&quot; would entail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T22:19:47-07:00","id":1087518,"title":"","content":"Now that c20 is out and we have how new Kithain come into existence. During the Ressurgence a certain species of Chimera evolved into full on Kithain. We also know now that points of particular hope and dream open the gates to Arcadia briefly and let more Changelings through from there(particularly Sidhe).<br /> <br /> So if you catch one of those Openings from Arcadia and have I'd imagine Prime 5, Mind(something) Spirit 5, time at least 2 to properly align with the point and some level of entropy to help with tweaking destiny. Of course you may not need to have them all on the same Mage. While the person doing the soul tweaking needs Mind prime, and spirit, Time alignment might be setup by another as might the Entropy tweaking.<br /> <br /> There will probably be all sorts of horrific feedback from the dreaming/Mists over it but PLOT!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T23:03:02-07:00","id":1087530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1084992-how-do-you-do-that-transform-kinain-into-kithain?p=1087518#post1087518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that c20 is out and we have how new Kithain come into existence. During the Ressurgence a certain species of Chimera evolved into full on Kithain. We also know now that points of particular hope and dream open the gates to Arcadia briefly and let more Changelings through from there(particularly Sidhe).<br /> <br /> So if you catch one of those Openings from Arcadia and have I'd imagine Prime 5, Mind(something) Spirit 5, time at least 2 to properly align with the point and some level of entropy to help with tweaking destiny. Of course you may not need to have them all on the same Mage. While the person doing the soul tweaking needs Mind prime, and spirit, Time alignment might be setup by another as might the Entropy tweaking.<br /> <br /> There will probably be all sorts of horrific feedback from the dreaming/Mists over it but PLOT!</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, you'll probably need to wrangle shitloads of Quintessence. Just getting a long-term enchantment on a mortal requires 20 Glamour and a lengthy ritual, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"at